# happens instead is a HANDOVER, and the list below was MEASURED by diffing this proof's declared
# literals against the seventh's rather than recalled — the first draft of this paragraph named the
# wrong three, omitting README.md's and claiming a CLAUDE.md pair that had in fact been merged.
#
# Three of the seventh trim's literals are now read, verbatim and unchanged, by L14:
#   * `BACKLOG.md`'s "`SESSION_NOTES-S238-through-S236.md` (644 lines)"   (was L12/prose's)
#   * `README.md`'s "Sessions 238->236 (grep it; do not Read it)"          (was L13/prose's)
#   * `PROJECT_CONVENTIONS.md`'s "(Session 242, Sessions 238→236)"         (was L13/prose's)
# One PAIR is MERGED rather than moved: `CLAUDE.md`'s ", 644 lines), each beside its own" (L12's)
# and "`SESSION_NOTES-S238-through-S236.md` (238→236" (L13's) are a single L14 literal now,
# "`SESSION_NOTES-S238-through-S236.md` (238→236, 644 lines)", carrying both fields. The seventh
# trim had to SPLIT that string to give L13 a mutant of its own; L14 reads both fields with separate
# ARMS inside one assertion, so the split is no longer needed and the two halves come back together.
# The rest of the seventh trim's declarations are SUPERSEDED, not dropped: each was about the cut
# that shipped it, and this cut declares its own equivalent. Reach is preserved in every case — the
# 1,057 and 644 figures by L14's BACKLOG chain literals, the S238 filename by L8/set.
#
# THE HANDOVER IS THE POINT. Doing it by hand is exactly the labour L14 exists to make unnecessary,
# and L14/set is what forces the NINTH trim to do it rather than inherit a green declaration.
#
# ONE MESSAGE STRING CHANGED AND NO LOGIC DID. L10's failure text said "six banners ... still tell
# readers to run this proof"; it says "seven" here. An `ast.unparse` diff of L0-L13 against the
# seventh proof, with comments and docstrings stripped, shows that string and the declared L13
