# ***
# *** WHAT IS PUBLISHED ABOVE IS COMPLETE AND WAS MEASURED ON THESE ARTIFACTS: the whole-assertion
# *** neuter loop, all fifteen assertions, against all 95 mutants.
# ***
# *** THE NINTH TRIM MUST RUN THE ARM SWEEP BEFORE TRUSTING THIS PROOF, and should treat its result
# *** as a finding to publish. Neuter one failure-emitting statement at a time — `out.append(...)`
# *** to `pass`, and `return [...]` to `return []`, which is type-preserving and is why the second
# *** run had to be redone — re-run `--self-test` for each, and record which mutants survive. An
# *** arm that no mutant reaches is an arm that has never fired. Freeze the artifacts for the whole
# *** run, and assert the exit code is 0 or 2; anything else is a broken run, not a clean one.
#
# The grammar is FROZEN into this file on purpose: a later change to the trim design must not
# silently change what THIS shard's proof means.
